{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 3,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.046,
            0.367,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.088,
            0.846,
            0.124
          ],
          "content": "Can we also think of an odd number as one less than a collection of pairs?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.124,
            0.815,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": "This figure shows that the sum of two odd numbers must always be even! This along with the other figures here are more examples of a **proof**!"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.823,
            0.12,
            0.865,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.287,
            0.206,
            0.698,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_3_image_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.415,
            0.847,
            0.456
          ],
          "content": "? What about adding 3 odd numbers? Can the resulting sum be arranged in pairs? No."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.475,
            0.847,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "Explore what happens to the sum of (a) 4 odd numbers, (b) 5 odd numbers, and (c) 6 odd numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.525,
            0.848,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "Let us go back to the puzzle Kishor was trying to solve. There are 5 empty boxes. That means he has an odd number of boxes. All the number cards contain odd numbers."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.58,
            0.848,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": "They should add to 30, which is an even number. Since, adding any 5 odd numbers will never result in an even number, Kishor cannot arrange these cards in the boxes to add up to 30."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.645,
            0.848,
            0.705
          ],
          "content": "Two siblings, Martin and Maria, were born exactly one year apart. Today they are celebrating their birthday. Maria exclaims that the sum of their ages is 112. Is this possible? Why or why not?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.713,
            0.848,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": "As they were born one year apart, their ages will be (two) consecutive numbers. Can their ages be 51 and 52? 51 + 52 = 103. Try some other consecutive numbers and see if their sum is 112."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.768,
            0.848,
            0.824
          ],
          "content": "The counting numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, ... alternate between even and odd numbers. In any two consecutive numbers, one will always be even and the other will always be odd!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.823,
            0.848,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": "What would be the resulting sum of an even number and an odd number? We can see that their sum can’t be arranged in pairs and thus will be an odd number."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.938,
            0.194,
            0.955
          ],
          "content": "130"
        },
